1. Multiple except Clauses

You can stack multiple except blocks so that different exception species receive their own tailored recovery procedure.
 * Order Matters: Catch specific/narrow exceptions before broader ones. If a broad parent exception comes first, it will catch errors intended for more specific clauses underneath.
try:
    process_record(line)
except ValueError:
    # Handles invalid data formats
    log_warning("Bad numerical format")
except IndexError:
    # Handles missing columns/fields
    log_warning("Incomplete log line")

2. Pulling the Andon Cord — Raising Exceptions (raise)

Just as an assembly line worker pulls the Andon cord to stop production when a defect occurs, your program uses raise to intentionally throw an error the moment a violation is detected.
Creating Custom Exception Classes
