> Why Inherit from Built-in Exceptions? Inheriting from ValueError guarantees that code already written to catch standard ValueErrors will automatically catch your custom SpecViolation as well.

3. Engineering Judgment: Log & Continue vs. Stop the Line
A robust program does not mean one that never fails—it fails in the right place, loudly, with the rest of the production line still running safely.
4. Key Takeaways
 * Raise Instantly: Use raise the moment your code detects invalid conditions—not three functions later when evidence is lost.
 * Selective Catching: Decide intentionally which faults your program should handle silently and which faults it should refuse to handle and let crash.
